{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1189290-twilight-caste-for-newbie","id":1189290,"title":"Twilight Caste for Newbie?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-24T14:46:01-08:00","id":1189290,"title":"Twilight Caste for Newbie?","content":"I've been a long time admirer and reader of the Exalted setting but starting with second edition I had been a little too intimidated by the setting to ever actually play. Well, that is going to change soon with a game I am about to take part in but I had some concerns that my favored Caste, Twilight, might not be the best role to start out with since it adds the magic system onto the core I already have to get used too. I was wondering if anyone that had experience running games with new players noticed Twilight being particularly difficult and if so what sort of Caste tends to do best for newbies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:18:54-08:00","id":1189295,"title":"","content":"Bear in mind that the sorcery system isn't something all Twilights do. One of our Twilights didn't pick up sorcery until he was Essence 5, and the other never bought it. In our group, the sorcerers are the Eclipse and the Changing Moon.<br /> <br /> Twilights could be:<br /> crafters<br /> teachers<br /> shamans<br /> doctors<br /> detectives<br /> writers<br /> bureaucrats<br /> sages<br /> philosophers<br /> And much more.<br /> <br /> If you want to be a doctor, I don't think playing a Twilight is very complicated. Same goes for detective, occultist, etc.<br /> <br /> Being a crafter is quite complicated though. I'm not sure I'd recommend it for new players, if they're not very confident of the mechanics. It's a whole new system to learn, and that's a system that has a lot of parts to it.<br /> <br /> Sorcery is a little more complicated than not having it, but it's not that complicated. I'd argue that frequently, playing a sorcerer might be easier than playing, say, a Dawn, because a Dawn is deciding how many and in what combination to use his or her 6-20 attack-enhancing charms on each attack.<br /> Whereas, when you cast a spell, the only thing you're going to combine with it is excellencies.<br /> <br /> Do you have any particular concept for this Twilight?<br /> <br /> Overall, I wouldn't say Twilight is the hardest caste to play for new players. I'd say it's probably Dawn, because there's a lot of interlocking parts (especially if you're combining Melee/Brawl and Martial Arts, because the restrictions on when you can and can't combine them often confuses players). But I don't think Dawn's much harder to play than any other caste (and it depends a lot on what charms you take. If you've got 5 ox-bodies, that's very straight-forward), and the others are about the same.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-24T15:21:21-08:00","id":1189296,"title":"","content":"First, which edition are you playing?<br /> <br /> Second, Twilight castes are not necessarily required to be Sorcerers, so they might not be as complex as you think. What do you like about Twilights?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:02:59-08:00","id":1189413,"title":"","content":"Yeah I'm aware of the diversity within the Castes. Night Caste is probably my second favorite option just for that reason. But with Twilight's I am drawn to the epic sorcerer angle. On the road to that he's likely going to be a sort of frustrated scholar/teacher. From the original Caste books I always liked Horakinis (think I'm spelling that right) who was a bit elitist but their mission, along with self-discovery/growth was spreading knowledge. The crafting aspect of Twilight's never appealed to me personally, not being a big tech/engineering person in real life. In Apocalypse I tend to play Theurge. And the game I've done the most is Mage the Awakening, so its how I lean.<br /> <br /> We are going to be playing Third Edition, which at first glance does seem a bit more complicated than even Second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1007-merinoc","name":"Merinoc","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T09:20:28-08:00","id":1189416,"title":"","content":"If you're about the epic sorcery, not the crafting, I think you'll find sorcery fine. It's simpler than a combat or social-fu character, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-25T10:27:54-08:00","id":1189429,"title":"","content":"In your case then, I would suggest going Lore or Occult Supernal and buying Sorcery. And, if you can handle Mage, then I'm confident you can deal with the complexity of this system.<br /> <br /> ....Though, if you do go for the teaching charms in Lore, the ones that let you mess with xp totals, those can get a bit complicated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}